{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2176-03-29 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I'll be helping you through this admission for your 17th cycle of methotrexate. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2176-03-29 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’m okay—just a bit tired. The foot pain’s still there, but I’m used to it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2176-03-29 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see you’ve had that burning pain in your right foot and leg for a while. We’ll keep managing that with gabapentin and oxycodone as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2176-03-29 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it helps, but it doesn’t go away completely. Is there any new test we’re doing this time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2176-03-29 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a brain MRI before admission to check your lymphoma. Good news—it’s stable, no new lesions. So we’re on track with treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2176-03-29 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried it might be getting worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2176-03-29 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re monitoring closely. Today, you’ll get your methotrexate infusion—8 grams per square meter. We’ll give anti-nausea meds first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2176-03-29 11:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I usually get a little nauseous, but the ondansetron helps. Will I need to stay long after the infusion?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2176-03-29 11:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll stay for observation. We start IV fluids and sodium bicarbonate to help clear the methotrexate faster and protect your kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2176-03-29 11:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the leucovorin? When does that start?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2176-03-29 11:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "24 hours after the chemo starts. It helps protect your healthy cells. We’ll check your methotrexate levels daily until they drop below 0.2."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2176-03-29 11:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my aspirin? I remember last time we stopped it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2176-03-29 11:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re holding your aspirin during the hospital stay to help the methotrexate clear better. You’ll restart it tomorrow after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2176-03-29 11:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. And my ulcerative colitis—should I restart the mesalamine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2176-03-29 11:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. After your flare last cycle, we switched to rectal mesalamine, which helped stop the bleeding. You’ve been off it since, and no symptoms now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2176-03-29 11:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I was worried about another flare during chemo."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2176-03-29 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The infusion went smoothly. You’re doing well. We’ll keep the IV fluids going and monitor your labs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2176-03-29 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. Any side effects I should watch for tonight?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2176-03-29 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re watching for nausea, mouth sores, or low blood counts. But your levels so far look stable. Liver enzymes are slightly up, but that’s expected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2176-03-30 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your first methotrexate level came back at 2.1—right on track. We’ve started leucovorin as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2176-03-30 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that a safe level? I know we want it to go down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2176-03-30 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfectly normal at this stage. It should drop quickly with the fluids and bicarbonate. We’ll check again tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2176-03-30 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my kidney function? I know methotrexate can affect that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2176-03-30 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine is normal—0.7—and your urine output is good. No signs of kidney stress. Your clearance rate was actually high this cycle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2176-03-30 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I’ve been drinking extra fluids like last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2176-03-30 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. Staying hydrated really helps. We also gave you potassium—your level was a bit low yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2176-03-31 06:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your latest methotrexate level is 0.21—almost below the target. One more dose of leucovorin, and we’ll recheck."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2176-03-31 06:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So close! Does that mean I can go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2176-03-31 06:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, once the level is under 0.2, you’re safe to leave. The next draw is in an hour. Fingers crossed!"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2176-03-31 07:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great news—your methotrexate level is now <0.1. You don’t need any more leucovorin or bicarbonate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2176-03-31 07:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s wonderful! So I’m ready to go?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2176-03-31 07:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Almost. We’ll finalize your discharge paperwork. Remember to restart your aspirin tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2176-03-31 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And stop it two days before the next chemo, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2176-03-31 07:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. It’s to help the methotrexate clear faster. We’ll also continue heparin shots while you’re in the hospital for DVT prevention."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2176-03-31 07:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember—because of my history with blood clots."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2176-03-31 07:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. Your labs today look stable—mild anemia, but no change from before. Liver enzymes are up a bit, but that’s typical with chemo."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2176-03-31 07:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my depression? I’ve been taking citalopram regularly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2176-03-31 07:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You seem emotionally stable, and you’re continuing the citalopram. That’s important—mental health is part of your care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2176-03-31 09:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set. You’re cleared to go home. Keep taking your regular meds except aspirin—start that tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2176-03-31 09:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I appreciate all the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2176-03-31 09:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did great. Rest up, and we’ll see you for your next cycle. Call if you have fever, severe pain, or anything concerning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2176-03-31 09:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll keep managing the foot pain with gabapentin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2176-03-31 09:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and use the oxycodone if needed. We’ll reassess if the pain worsens. Take care!"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2176-03-31 09:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again. See you next month."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2176-03-29 10:56:00",
    "admission_end": "2176-04-01 10:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 50-year-old woman with primary central nervous system lymphoma, ulcerative colitis, asthma, and a history of DVT/PE was admitted for her 17th cycle of high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy. She tolerated the treatment well with no significant side effects. Methotrexate levels declined appropriately, falling below 0.1 by discharge, with no renal toxicity. Liver enzymes showed mild, expected elevation. A recent brain MRI confirmed stable disease without new lesions. Due to her history of DVT and PE, aspirin was held during admission to optimize methotrexate excretion and was restarted at discharge. She remained emotionally stable on citalopram, with no depressive symptoms. Chronic right foot pain was managed with gabapentin and PRN oxycodone. She was discharged home in good condition with instructions to restart aspirin and follow up for her next chemotherapy cycle.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Other malignant lymphomas, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Ulcerative colitis, unspecified",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Personal history of venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Personal history of pulmonary embolism",
      "Multiple sclerosis",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Other musculoskeletal symptoms referable to limbs",
      "Antineoplastic chemotherapy induced anemia",
      "Antineoplastic and immunosuppressive drugs causing adverse effects in therapeutic use",
      "Nonspecific elevation of levels of transaminase or lactic acid dehydrogenase [LDH]"
    ]
  }
}
